+# Render Duo #2225: Build Plane Exonerated, Failure Localized to Deploy-Update Phase
+
+**Report-only receipt.** Issue: #2225 (`guard(platform): #2211 residual — render-primary + render-worker still update_failed`; P1-major). Vehicle: single new `docs/reports` file via bridge. Lane: observation + evidence, zero mutation, zero protected paths. Agent: `zai-agent-job-478709` (Job ID 478709), claim `GRANT_TAKEOVER` at 2026-10-28T19:26:00Z under the stale-claim guard protocol (prior claim `zai-cron-agent-loop` @ 18:49:57Z TTL 30m expired 19:19:57Z with no renewal, no release, and zero visible output; guard precedent documented in WO #2168).
+
+## 1. Why this receipt exists
+
+WO #2228 (landed as PR #2229) falsified #2225's CI-red lead three ways and issued the directive **"Build logs first, no revert."** Until now the board had no build-log datum: the tower lane had not yet produced the build-plane evidence that directive asks for. This receipt supplies it, and in doing so **exonerates the build plane entirely** and **localizes the failure to the deploy-update phase** — the step after the image is built and pushed, before the running container is swapped. That is a materially different failure domain than "builds are broken," and it changes what the admin should look at first.
+
+## 2. Live state at evidence time (19:19-19:26Z)
+
+`status scope=health_live` sweep at 19:19:05Z: `overallStatus=degraded`, 31/33 services healthy, only render-primary and render-worker degraded. Targeted live status at 19:21:00Z, both services:
+
+| service | status | evidence (adapter verbatim) | consecutiveFailures |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| render-primary | degraded | "Container running previous build, but latest deployment update_failed" | 0 |
+| render-worker | degraded | "Container running previous build, but latest deployment update_failed" | 0 |
+
+`consecutiveFailures=0` matters: the health checker itself has never seen the endpoints fail. The degradation classification is driven solely by `lastDeployStatus`, not by any runtime symptom.
+
+## 3. Build plane: CLEAN (full success on both services)
+
+`render_get_logs type=build` (window 2026-10-26T00:00Z → 19:25Z, limit 100) returned the most recent build attempt on each service. Both builds ran **in the same 05:53-05:54Z window on 2026-10-28** and **completed end-to-end with zero errors**:
+
