+| #17 export build cache | DONE 43.6s | DONE 39.3s |
+
+The last log lines on both are `#17 DONE` — the Docker build pipeline reached its final step. **No build error exists to fix.** A ~14-minute starter-plan build (800+ s of it pip install) that finishes clean and still ends in `update_failed` means the failure happens **after** image push, in Render's deploy/update/rollout machinery.
+
+## 4. Runtime plane: CLEAN
+
+- `render_get_logs type=app level=error`, window 2026-10-25T00:00Z → 19:25Z: **0 rows** on render-primary. Three and a half days with zero error-severity runtime logs.
+- App logs show `GET /health/live 200 OK` every 5 s continuously through the evidence window (19:16-19:19Z sampled), consistent with the adapter's "container running previous build" and `consecutiveFailures=0`.
+- The duo is not degraded in any runtime sense; they are frozen on the previous build while every new deploy attempt dies at update phase.
+
